To-Do

	- Remove obsolete bits such as uu for particles, etc.


Bugs (see also patch/tepper/oagertz/dice_restart/README)

    - Main step starts at 1 instead of at the actual last value at restart; the same is true for nstep_coarse.

    - When loading additional DICE ICs, there may be a potential issue with duplicate particle ids (iord)

    - Gas particle (cell) number and gas mass increases slightly at restart, presumably due to the fact that IG_rho != 0

    - Some particles end up at or beyond the box boundary at restart
    The fix for now is to toss these, which is not fully consistent with the restart snapshot state


Modifications
** Note that not all modifications are detailed as they are, but they can be easily searched for with the information provided

    read_params.f90:
    - added module 'dice_restart_commons' (called restart_commons pre JUL2025)
    - added subroutine 'read_dice_restart_params()', which includes the declaration of the NML block dice_restart_params (called restart_params pre JUL2025).
    IMPORTANT: Note that this requires to update all relevant NML files in patch/tepper/namelist -> DONE
    - added the strings '! DICE patch' and '! DICE_RESTART patch' to several locations to distinguish between the snippets particular to each of thee patches
    - added verification of some dice_restart_params parameters to subroutine read_run_params()

    init_part.f90:
    - added subroutine load_ramses_dice and corresponding:
        case ('ramses_dice')
            call load_ramses_dice
    - added to subroutine load_dice the following:
        use restart_commons, only: restart_init
    and some related checks (look for dice_restart_init)
